        "description": "<figure>\n\n<img alt=\"Xbox ex boss Phil Spencer seated on a coach with new Xbox CEO Asha Sharma\" data-caption=\"Xbox ex boss and new Xbox boss | Image: Microsoft\" data-portal-copyright=\"Image: Microsoft\" data-has-syndication-rights=\"1\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/02/image-7.jpg?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\" />\n\t<figcaption>\n\tXbox ex boss and new Xbox boss | Image: Microsoft\t</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p class=\"has-text-align-none\">After nearly 40 years at Microsoft, Xbox chief and Microsoft Gaming CEO Phil Spencer is leaving the company, along with Xbox president Sarah Bond. Spencer\u2019s retirement was <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/news/882241/microsoft-phil-spencer-xbox-leaving-retirement\">announced in a memo</a> from Microsoft CEO Satya Nadella on February 20th, stating, \u201cLast year, Phil Spencer made the decision to retire from the company, and since then we\u2019ve been talking about succession planning.\u201d&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p class=\"has-text",
